.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_ACERT_ADD_ATTR_NCONF 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_ACERT_add_attr_nconf
.Nd Add attributes to X509_ACERT from configuration section
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509_acert.h
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_add_attr_nconf
.Fa "CONF *conf"
.Fa "const char *section"
.Fa "X509_ACERT *acert"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_ACERT_add_attr_nconf
adds one or more
.Sy X509_ATTRIBUTE Ns s
to the existing
.Vt X509_ACERT
structure
.Fa acert .
The attributes are read from a
.Fa section
of the
.Fa conf
object.
.Pp
The give
.Fa section
of the configuration should contain attribute descriptions of the form:
.Bd -literal
  attribute_name = value
.Ed
.Pp
The format of
.Sy value
will vary depending on the
.Sy attribute_name .
.Sy value
can either be a string value or an
.Sy ASN1_TYPE
object.
.Pp
To encode an
.Sy ASN1_TYPE
object, use the prefix "ASN1:" followed by the object description that
uses the same syntax as
.Xr ASN1_generate_nconf 3 .
For example:
.Bd -literal
 id-aca-group = ASN1:SEQUENCE:ietfattr

 [ietfattr]
 values = SEQUENCE:groups

 [groups]
 1.string = UTF8:mygroup1
.Ed
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_ACERT_add_attr_nconf
returns 1 for success and 0 for failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ASN1_generate_nconf 3 .
.Sh HISTORY
The function
.Fn X509_ACERT_add_attr_nconf
was added in OpenSSL 3.4.
